  <div class="section-label jump-target" id="project-timeline">Project Timeline</div>
  <h2>Chronological Progression</h2>

  <ol class="timeline">
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2024-01">January 2024</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 1 Opens</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">16-mile West Davis Highway (Farmington to SR-193 in West Point) opens to traffic. $750M project completed.{% cite "udot-wdc-overview" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2025-11">November 2025</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Weber County State Environmental Study Scoping Meeting</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Public Scoping Meeting held November 20, 2025. State Environmental Study formally launched for 1800 N → 4000 S segment.{% cite "udot-scoping-nov2025" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2025-12">December 2025</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 2 Utility Work Begins</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Preliminary utility relocations begin in Davis County along SR-193 → 1800 N alignment. Rocky Mountain Power, Hooper Water, Canal Company crews active.{% cite "se-extension-davis-start" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2026-04">Spring 2026</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">State Environmental Study Alternatives Development</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Weber County State Environmental Study moves into Alternatives Development and Evaluation. Build Alternative footprint mapping is underway, and public working technical layers now show related concept-design data for the 5100 West study corridor.{% cite "udot-ses-build" %}{% cite "arcgis-sr177-project-layers-may2026" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2026-06">Summer 2026</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 2 Major Construction Begins</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">$225M Phase 2 extension (SR-193 → 1800 N) enters full construction. Land clearing, earthmoving, drainage, paving through 2028.{% cite "udot-2026-construction" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item future">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2026-11-06">Nov 6 – Dec 11, 2026</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Draft State Environmental Study and Public Comment Period</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">UDOT published the Draft State Environmental Study online on November 6, 2026, with the first formal alignment and right-of-way maps for the Weber County segment. Its Preferred Alternative is a four-lane freeway along 5100 West with interchanges at 1800 North, 5500 South, and 4000 South.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %} The formal comment period runs through December 11. The online presentation was held November 9 and the in-person public hearing was set for November 10 at Roy Junior High School.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}{% cite "udot-ses-public-hearing-nov2026" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item future">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2027">Early 2027</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Final State Environmental Study</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">UDOT responds to public comments, then publishes the Final State Environmental Study for approval; UDOT says it is expected in early 2027 (its timeline graphic still shows "Late 2026/Early 2027").{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %} If approved, the project can move into design. No construction funding is allocated at this stage.</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item future speculative">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2028">2028–2029</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 2 Completion</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Phase 2 scheduled for completion late 2028 to early 2029. SR-177 terminus reaches 1800 North in West Point.</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item future speculative">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2033">2033–2042 (Regional Plan)</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 3 Construction Window in the Regional Plan</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">The Wasatch Front Regional Council 2023–2050 Regional Transportation Plan lists the 1800 North to 4000 South extension as new construction in its Phase 2 (2033–2042), an assumed-funding window rather than a funding commitment; the Draft State Environmental Study confirms that placement.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}{% cite "wfrc-rtp-2023-2050" %} Earlier versions of this site placed it in 2043–2050, which applies to the segment north of 4000 South.{% cite "wfrc-rtp-roadway-lines-2023" %} UDOT's draft 2027–2032 construction program includes no construction money for this segment.{% cite "udot-draft-stip-2027-2032" %} Weber County officials have lobbied for acceleration.{% cite "ksl-weber-officials-favor" %}</div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout warning">
    <p><strong>Funding gap:</strong> Construction of the Weber County extension is not currently funded. The draft study says it could be built in two phases "as funding becomes available": first the 1800 North interchange and the extension to 5500 South, then the 5500 South interchange and the extension to 4000 South, with the 4000 South interchange "reevaluated and constructed as part of a future UDOT project."{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %} Building any phase sooner than the regional plan assumes would require UDOT and the Legislature to allocate significant funding.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-label jump-target" id="davis-precedent">Analog Comparison</div>
  <h2>Davis County Precedent</h2>

  <p>The Davis County West Davis Corridor provides the nearest historical analog:</p>

  <ul style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.2;">
    <li>Environmental Impact Statement completed: <strong>2017</strong>{% cite "udot-wdc-overview" %}</li>
    <li>Construction funding secured and design finalized: <strong>~2020–2021</strong></li>
    <li>Construction commenced: <strong>Early 2021</strong></li>
    <li>Open to traffic: <strong>January 2024</strong>{% cite "udot-wdc-overview" %}</li>
    <li><strong>Total: approximately 7 years from Environmental Impact Statement completion to opening</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <p>The Davis County project moved from Environmental Impact Statement completion to opening in roughly seven years because funding was secured promptly. The Weber County State Environmental Study is expected to conclude in early 2027.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %} If construction funding were secured immediately afterward — a scenario not supported by UDOT's draft 2027–2032 program{% cite "udot-draft-stip-2027-2032" %} — an equivalent interval would suggest a possible opening no earlier than the early 2030s. The draft study's traffic analysis uses 2032 as an assumed opening year; that is a modeling assumption, not a schedule.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %} Under the current regional plan, construction is placed in the 2033–2042 window.</p>

  <div class="section-label jump-target" id="funding-scenarios">Funding Scenarios</div>
  <h2>Realistic Timelines Based on Funding Status</h2>

  <p>The Phase 3 construction timeline depends critically on when (and if) funding is allocated. Below are three scenarios based on the Davis County precedent (approximately 7 years from Environmental Impact Statement completion to opening):</p>

  <table>
    <caption>Phase 3 construction timeline scenarios</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Scenario</th>
        <th scope="col">Funding Secured</th>
        <th scope="col">Design Phase</th>
        <th scope="col">Construction Start</th>
        <th scope="col">Est. Opening</th>
        <th scope="col">Current Likelihood</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Accelerated</strong></td>
        <td>Late 2026 / Early 2027</td>
        <td>2027–2029</td>
        <td>2029–2030</td>
        <td>2032–2033</td>
        <td>Very low (no construction money in UDOT's draft 2027–2032 program)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Expedited</strong></td>
        <td>2030</td>
        <td>2030–2032</td>
        <td>2032–2033</td>
        <td>2035–2036</td>
        <td>Low (requires legislative priority)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Regional Plan</strong></td>
        <td>2033 (or later)</td>
        <td>2033–2035</td>
        <td>2035–2036</td>
        <td>2038–2042</td>
        <td>Current regional-plan assumption (Phase 2, 2033–2042); not a funding commitment</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p><strong>Key takeaway:</strong> Property owners should plan for a long timeline. The adopted regional plan assumes construction in 2033–2042, but no construction money is programmed through 2032, and the regional council's next plan (2027–2055) could move the project earlier or later. The draft study's two-phase approach means the southern part (1800 North to 5500 South) could be built before the part from 5500 South to 4000 South.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}{% cite "udot-draft-stip-2027-2032" %} Funded right-of-way acquisition would not begin until money is allocated and design starts; voluntary corridor-preservation purchases can happen earlier.</p>
